# Example of the build-time settings the envi CLI is usually built with.
#
#   cp .env.cli.example .env.cli
#   make build-envi
#
# .env.cli is what actually gets read — this file is only here to show the
# shape of it. Each key is the name of a Go variable in internal/cli, injected
# with -ldflags -X at build time, so a key is only useful if that variable
# exists. Anything not listed in .env.cli keeps the default compiled into the
# source.
#
# The release pipeline writes its own .env.cli from the repository secret, so
# these values never reach a published binary.

# Which API the CLI talks to. Without it, an unstamped build falls back to
# http://127.0.0.1:8080 and a released build to the hosted service.
DefaultAPIURL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
